# Negative fixture (derive contract): `#[derive(Json)]` accepts a sum
# type under the adjacently-tagged envelope, but every variant payload
# must be JSON-bindable. A generic payload has no monomorphic
# `of_json` shim, so it is rejected at the derive, naming the offending
# variant — the same located contract a record field gets.

#[derive(Json)]
type Event = Tick | Fire(Result[Int, String])

fn main() : Int = 0
